Bugfix: Enforce `--max-size` for config uploads

Uploading a repository `config` file bypassed the repository size limit set
with `--max-size`. A client could create new (sub-)repositories and upload
arbitrarily large `config` files into them to fill up the disk. The uploaded
bytes were also missing from the size tally used to enforce the limit until
rest-server was restarted.

Config uploads are now subject to the size limit and are rejected with HTTP
status `507 Insufficient Storage` when they would exceed it, just like other
uploads. Deleting a config now frees the space in the size tally. In addition,
a config file may not be larger than 1 MiB; larger uploads are rejected with
HTTP status `413 Request Entity Too Large`.

https://github.com/restic/rest-server/issues/407
